# The idle timer as a state machine. Positions are grid cells: at <col> <row>.
title:   How idle-compact decides when to compact
caption: When Claude finishes replying, idle-compact starts a countdown, and your next message cancels it. If the countdown runs out, the conversation is compacted, but only when it is big enough to be worth it.
note:    After any outcome the timer rests until Claude finishes its next reply. The numbers shown are the defaults: 20 minutes and 120,000 tokens are both settings.

start  session  at 0 -0.8
start  tool     at -0.3 1
state  idle     Resting — no countdown running        at 0 0    mute
state  armed    Counting down — 20 minutes by default  at 1 0    violet
state  check    Size check — is it big enough?        at 2 0    amber
state  done     Compacted — and you are notified      at 3 -1   green
state  skip     Left alone — too small to matter      at 3 0    mute
state  dry      Dry run — a report, no change         at 3 1    mute
state  queued   Requested — waits for the reply to end  at 1 1    teal

session -> idle   a session starts
idle -> armed     Claude finishes replying  bend 22
armed -> idle     you send a message  bend 22
armed -> armed    another reply ends, or a setting changes
armed -> check    time is up
check -> done     big enough
check -> skip     too small
check -> dry      big enough, dry run on
tool -> queued    Claude asks to compact now  dashed
queued -> check   1 second after the reply ends  dashed  bend -8

term  Compact — Claude Code replaces the conversation so far with a short summary of it, so there is far less to re-read.
term  Big enough — the conversation holds at least 120,000 tokens (a token is a small piece of text, roughly three quarters of a word). Smaller conversations are cheap to re-read, so they are left alone.
term  Notified — a short message on screen, a line in the mod's log, and a notification on your phone or desktop.
term  Dry run — a setting for trying the mod out: it reports what it would have done and changes nothing.
term  Claude asks to compact now — idle-compact gives Claude a tool for this (compact_after_turn). Ask Claude to "compact after this turn" and it skips the wait and the size check.
term  Session — one conversation with Claude Code, on your computer or in the cloud.
